<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<x3ml xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      source_type="xpath"
      version="1.0"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://isl.ics.forth.gr/x3ml/schema/x3ml.xsd">
   <info>
      <title>SemantyFish_REPRODUCTION_Table_</title>
      <general_description>Mappings for the table ECOLOGY of FishBase

i've switched back to almost exclusively using marine-tlo classes and properties. ISA relations have been substituted for Part_Of relations (btw types) to ensure that only marine-tlo is used. where P2 has type:E55 Type occurs it's for things that fall outside the scope of the classifications by fishbase (potentially redundant types --namely: "aquatic ecosystems", "type of substrate", "special habitats". Also "feeding type" and "feeding behavior" for trophic levels. What these P2:E55 chains all have in common, is that they can be deleted without loss of meaning. </general_description>
      <source>
